From 2e60929aafc2454595f695bb56a949904b813ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:49:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] Support \caption* with an \@caption that a class
 replaced

Classes and packages that replace \@caption by a definition that does
not know the star (llncs, mwcls, jpsj2, ...) typeset \fnum@<type> with
the number of the previous caption, write a list entry and, with
hyperref, may make a target named after the previous caption. For
\caption*, \@caption@nostep@defs therefore lets \fnum@<type> be
\@caption@nolabel, makes \ext@<type> empty and gives \theH<type> a
unique suffix (for a caption that does not step its counter only the
suffix). The settings last until the next \caption, the end of the
group, or the start of the kernel \@caption, because \@caption has to
stay the last token of \caption and a replaced \@caption may defer its
work (threeparttable). The kernel \@caption gives an unused unique
number back. \if@captionstar stays true until the same point. That is
a trade-off: a \@makecaption that runs later in the same group without
a \caption before it (e.g., for a listing) would also omit its label,
so clsguide asks a class whose \@caption handles \caption* itself to
set the switch false at its end.

\@kernel@caption@reset now also ends these settings. It is documented
for code that keeps its own numbered \caption and passes only \caption*
to the kernel with \@kernel@caption* (clsguide).
\@kernel@caption@unique also works while the settings are active.

This part needs the previous one (the unique names of
\@caption@uniqueH). It is not optional for float.sty and hyperref: the
float first aid lets float's caption code act as a replaced \@caption
in restyled floats (algorithm.sty, \newfloat and \restylefloat types),
and classic hyperref replaces \@caption too. Without this part
\caption*{Starred} in a ruled algorithm gives "Algorithm 1 Starred"
(the number of the previous caption) with a list entry, a hyperref
that keeps its \caption and passes only \caption* to
\@kernel@caption* gives "Figure 1: Starred" with a list entry and a
duplicate destination, and classes such as llncs and mwcls give
\caption* a numbered label and a list entry.

New test caption-interface-004 (a replaced, a wrapping and a deferring
\@caption, the give-back, the reset, \@kernel@caption@unique while the
settings are active). latex-lab float-024 gets a class \@caption that
makes its own target.
